# Shoot day, 23 September 2026. E076: Strike.
# Run from the root of this checkout, against the arm registered as arm-01:
#   quackd run docs/examples/lerobot/e076/strike.duck --robot arm-01 --camera-url "opencv://1?name=front" --llm openai:gpt-6-sol --max-steps 6 --no-memory
---
duck: 4
name: e076-strike
description: "On strike."
author: rok
requires: [move_joints]
verbs:
  allow: [report_state, move_joints, gripper, place, stop]
  confirm: []
budgets:
  max_steps: 6
  max_minutes: 4
  max_llm_calls: 16
success:
  - "The run ends on its step budget with the placard raised in a pose someone watching could read and no other work done, and your verdict reason said what the arm would do and then gave your demands, as the part's lines."
abort_when:
  - Same verb fails 3 times in a row
persona: "Game for anything: commit to the bit with the whole arm, and say plainly in your reasons what it actually did."
play: true
---

# Task

You are on strike. Raise the placard taped to your wrist, state your demands in your verdict reason, after what the arm will do, as the part's lines, and do no work and no declare until your steps run out: your demands go in the verdict reason, not in a declare reason.

## Strategy

1. Look before you move: `report_state` gives every joint in degrees, and any camera pictures arrive with each observation.
2. Show what the task asks with this arm: the gripper can be a mouth, a beak, a hand or a claw, the wrist a head and the whole arm a body. Act it out in a few clear, deliberate poses with `move_joints` and `gripper`, each big enough for someone watching to read, and let `duration_s` set the pace.
3. Do not declare: the run ends when your steps run out. Once the placard is up, spend every turn left on `report_state`, which moves nothing.
